<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ethiopian–Mahdist War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1885–1889</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Abyssinian–Sudanese War</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ethiopian–<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahdist-war">Mahdist War</a> was fought between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopian-empire">Ethiopian Empire</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahdist-state">Mahdist State</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sudan">Sudan</a>. After the Ethiopians helped evacuate Egyptian garrisons, Mahdist forces raided <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a> and sacked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gondar">Gondar</a> in 1888. At Gallabat, or Metemma, in March 1889 the Ethiopian army was winning when Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yohannes-iv">Yohannes IV</a> was mortally wounded, and it retreated in disorder.</p></div>
